{"tool_name":"multi-template-matching","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>Multi-template matching can be used to localize multiple objects using one or a set of template images.</p>\n\n<p>Contrary to previous implementations that allow to use only one template, here a set of templates can be used or the initial template(s) can be transformed by rotation/flipping.</p>\n\n<p>Multiple objects&nbsp;detection without redundant detections is possible thanks to a Non-Maxima Supression&nbsp;relying on the degree of overlap between detections.</p>\n\n<p>The solution is available as a Fiji plugin (Multi-Template Matching AND IJ-OpenCV update sites), as a Python package (Multi-Template-Matching on PyPI) and as a KNIME workflow (via KNIME Hub).</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>Multi-template matching can be used to localize multiple objects using one or a set of template images.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Contrary to previous implementations that allow to use only one template, here a set of templates can be used or the initial template(s) can be transformed by rotation/flipping.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Multiple objects&nbsp;detection without redundant detections is possible thanks to a Non-Maxima Supression&nbsp;relying on the degree of overlap between detections.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The solution is available as a Fiji plugin (Multi-Template Matching AND IJ-OpenCV update sites), as a Python package (Multi-Template-Matching on PyPI) and as a KNIME workflow (via KNIME Hub).</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2020-10-19T15:09:23+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2019-04-29T09:45:55+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":"","last_comment_timestamp":1603120163,"last_comment_uid":3113,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Thomas Laurent orcid.org/0000-0001-76